; FACING THE ROOM. Same defect the runner camera had, measured the same way:
; a headless probe of the real scene put the camera's forward at (0,-0.34,-0.94)
; while the rig sits at z=+14 and every piece of cover is at z=+4..+11, giving
; dot(forward, direction to rig) = -0.847. The rig, the cover and the Early
; Claim lever - the entire encounter - were BEHIND the camera.
;
; Basis: forward (0,-0.242,0.970) = down +Z pitched 14 degrees; right (-1,0,0);
; up (0,0.970,0.242). Moved from z=-5 to z=-9 so the bear that spawns at z=-6
; also starts in front of the player instead of behind their head.
[node name="Camera3D" type="Camera3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(-1, 0, 0, 0, 0.97, 0.242, 0, 0.242, -0.97, 0, 3.6, -9)

; Graybox lighting. Without a light and an environment a 3D scene renders unlit/black in the web export.
[node name="WorldEnvironment" type="WorldEnvironment" parent="."]
environment = SubResource("Environment_chamber")

[node name="Sun" type="DirectionalLight3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 0.7, 0.71, 0, -0.71, 0.7, 0, 10, 2)
light_energy = 0.75
shadow_enabled = true
